 @Gti_Jason  For suicide benchmarks... 4700c17 1t is atleast memorytest stable ;) 
In benchmarks I run 4800c17 1t very tight timings. Benching is fun :D
Looks like you also like extreme benchmarking ;)

 @SenderBudYerGood  And? I highly doubt when it comes to tech like this that anyone is buying a 3080, 3090 because of anything these guys say. I mean seriously are you gonna spend 700-1500 bucks based on what someone like Linus or Kyle or Jay tell you? If you are to me thats just sad. I know i didn't buy a 2080 TI because jay, or linus said they were good cards, i did it cuz i have the money and it was the top of the line. To me this kinda "advertising" is a waste of money. 

Maybe it works with the Ninja's and Dr. Disrespects of the world because they are "advertising" to impressionable children who are easily convinced to buy things simply because someone "famous" told them to. But i don't need these tech channels to tell me what i already know. 

Seriously you need to see Jay or Paul run 2 3090's in SLI for...what exactly? To convince you to buy a 3080 or 3090? For the lol's? For entertainment? I mean this video wasn't doing any of that to me. So what besides the sheer waste of components was this video trying to achieve?
